---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LabelChip from '../../../components/LabelChip.astro';
import ResultsExplorer from '../../../components/experiments/ResultsExplorer';
import { EXPERIMENTS } from '../../../lib/experiments/catalog';
import { loadExperiment, type ExperimentData } from '../../../lib/experiments/load';
import { formatValue, lossCases, verdict } from '../../../lib/experiments/data';
import { assetHref, pageHref } from '../../../lib/paths';
import { REPO_URL } from '../../../lib/site';
import '../../../components/experiments/results.css';
export async function getStaticPaths(){return Promise.all(EXPERIMENTS.map(async def=>({params:{experiment:def.slug},props:{data:await loadExperiment(def)}})));}
interface Props {data:ExperimentData}
const {data}=Astro.props;const def=data.definition;const manifest=data.manifest;const cases=lossCases(def,data.rows);
const sourcePath=`results/${def.id}/${def.run}/summary.csv`;
---
<BaseLayout evidenceOnly title={`${def.slug.toUpperCase()}: ${def.title}`} description={def.question}>
 <header class="page-hero container"><p class="eyebrow"><a href={pageHref('experiments')}>Experiments</a> / {def.slug.toUpperCase()}</p><h1>{def.title}</h1><p class="lede">{def.question}</p><div class="result-labels"><LabelChip kind="derived" note="statistics and accounting"/><LabelChip kind="modelled" note="network outcomes"/></div></header>
 <section class="section section--flush"><div class="container prose"><h2>Pre-registered hypothesis</h2><p>{def.hypothesis}</p><p><a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/${data.preregSha}/experiments/PREREG.md`}>Frozen preregistration</a>, identified and verified against this result’s manifest.</p><h2>Verdict</h2><p>{verdict(def,data.rows)}</p><p>C5 orbital inputs are REAL public data; C2 orbits and positions are MODELLED. Topology, probes, faults and network behaviour are MODELLED. Starlink’s operational routing is UNKNOWN; Starlink does not use T-CRH.</p></div></section>
 <section class="section" aria-labelledby="results-title"><div class="container"><h2 id="results-title">Charts and data</h2><p><a href={assetHref(`experiments/${def.slug}/summary.csv`)} download="summary.csv">Download CSV</a> · <a href={assetHref(`experiments/${def.slug}/manifest.json`)} download="manifest.json">Download manifest</a></p><p class="result-source">Source: <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/${sourcePath}`}><code>{sourcePath}</code></a>. SHA-256: <code>{data.summarySha}</code>.</p><ResultsExplorer definition={def} rows={data.rows} columns={data.columns} evidence={data.evidence} client:load/></div></section>
 <section class="section" aria-labelledby="losses-title"><div class="container"><h2 id="losses-title">Where ChronoRoute loses</h2><p>Every listed point disadvantage is retained, including privileged-oracle advantages. Marginal intervals alone do not establish an adjusted paired significant loss. Ties in the predicted stuck-loss reduction are listed as unsupported advantages.</p>{cases.length>0?<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable disadvantages table"><table><caption>Descriptive comparisons from the same summary; source row numbers count data rows, excluding the header.</caption><thead><tr>{['Cell','Metric','Policy','ChronoRoute','Comparator','Comparator value','Interpretation','Source rows'].map(h=><th scope="col">{h}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{cases.map(r=><tr><td>{r.context}</td><td>{r.metric}</td><td>{r.policy}</td><td>{formatValue(r.ours)}</td><td>{r.competitor}</td><td>{formatValue(r.theirs)}</td><td>{r.note}</td><td>{r.sourceRows}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>:<p>{def.id==='E16'?'No failed equivalence endpoint is recorded in this summary; this is a scoped agreement result, not a routing-performance win.':def.id==='E00'?'No correctness violation is recorded in this summary.':'No point disadvantage is identified by the displayed comparison metrics. This does not establish a universal advantage.'}</p>}</div></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2>Limitations</h2><ul>{def.limitations.map(text=><li>{text}</li>)}{typeof manifest.extra['limitations']==='string'&&<li>{manifest.extra['limitations']}</li>}</ul><p>These pages use only summary.csv and manifest.json. They do not infer missing comparisons from figures, reports, raw traces or other result files.</p></div></section>
 <section class="section" aria-labelledby="provenance-title"><div class="container"><h2 id="provenance-title">How this was made</h2><dl class="result-provenance"><dt>Recorded producer</dt><dd>{manifest.tool} ({manifest.tool_version})</dd><dt>Manifest commit</dt><dd><a href={`${REPO_URL}/commit/${manifest.git_sha}`}>{manifest.git_sha}</a>; dirty: {String(manifest.dirty)}</dd><dt>Run</dt><dd>{manifest.run_id}</dd><dt>Time</dt><dd>{manifest.started_utc} to {manifest.ended_utc}; {manifest.wall_seconds} seconds of recorded host wall time (REAL)</dd><dt>Snapshot</dt><dd>{manifest.snapshot?.id??'Not recorded'}; SHA-256: {manifest.snapshot?.sha256??'Not recorded'}</dd><dt>Seeds</dt><dd>{manifest.seeds.length?manifest.seeds.join(', '):'No random seed applies'}</dd><dt>Command</dt><dd><pre>{manifest.command}</pre></dd><dt>Config SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{manifest.config_sha256}</code></dd><dt>Labels</dt><dd><ul>{Object.entries(manifest.labels).map(([key,value])=><li>{key}: {value}</li>)}</ul>{typeof manifest.extra['synthetic_positions']==='string'&&<p>C2 override: {manifest.extra['synthetic_positions']}</p>}</dd></dl><p>For collected results, the manifest commit identifies the collector. Input hashes preserve the producer chain in the downloaded manifest; this page does not load those additional files.</p><details><summary>Full manifest: configuration, versions, host and input hashes</summary><pre>{data.manifestText}</pre></details></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
